\A{kitty-eventids} Windows Event Log event IDs

Each record carries its kind as insertion string \c{%1} and its fields
as \c{%2} onwards, in the order listed below; the message shows each
field as a \c{name: value} line, an absent field as an empty string.
Where kitty.exe is not registered as the message file of \c{KiTTY++}
(no system-wide installation), 900-903 are written as event ID 0 with
one readable line instead. The level of each ID is given in brackets.

The fields, by name:

\# BEGIN glossary generated by tools/check-kitty-events.py --write-appendix

\b \c{absent} - 113: startup keys whose file was not there.

\b \c{addr} - 200, 300: the address connected to (a proxy's when one is used); a serial line's name.

\b \c{basis} - 210, 310: how the host key was known; values: cache, manual, ca.

\b \c{bits} - 400: the key size in bits (255 for Ed25519, the curve size for ECDSA).

\b \c{broken} - 113: startup keys whose file could not be read.

\b \c{bytes} - 240, 241, 330, 331: the file's bytes moved; empty when not known.

\b \c{check} - 900: the check that refused the program file; values: rename, signature, integrity.

\b \c{comment} - 100-170: the comment of the key concerned; 400, 401: of the key generated or saved.

\b \c{credentials} - 225, 325: yes when a user name or password went to the proxy, else no.

\b \c{days} - 901: LogKeepDays as set, 0 = off.

\b \c{dest} - 131: the protected copy written.

\b \c{detail} - 130, 132: the detail Windows Hello reported; 230: the refusals the rate limit merged into this record (a number), open (a far2l clipboard open), the transfer id or the file name.

\b \c{direction} - 240, 241, 330, 331: put (upload, to the server) or get (download, from it).

\b \c{enc} - 111: whether the key file has a passphrase; values: password, blank.

\b \c{err} - 131: the error text when the protection failed.

\b \c{exitcode} - 201: the remote command's exit code; 301: the tool's own exit code; empty when there is none.

\b \c{features} - 902: the features this Windows lacks, comma-separated.

\b \c{files} - 901: the log files deleted.

\b \c{for} - 220, 221, 225, 320, 321, 325: what the connection served; empty for the connection's own login; session for a jump host's login and for a proxy the session went through; forward for a port forwarding's connection, x11 for an X11 forwarding's.

\b \c{format} - 401: ppk3, ppk2, openssh, ssh.com or ssh1; 402: rfc4716, openssh or ssh1.

\b \c{found} - 900: what the check found; rename: the program's file name; signature: bad digest, not signed, or signer: followed by the signer name; integrity: no stamp, truncated, bad stamp, modified or cannot check.

\b \c{fp} - the key fingerprint; 100-170: as the agent shows it (ssh-ed25519 255 SHA256:...; an SSH-1 key's bits and MD5 hash, 2048 aa:bb:...); 210-221, 310-321, 400-403: the hash alone (SHA256:...; an SSH-1 key's MD5 hash, aa:bb:...), empty for a proxy's login.

\b \c{from} - 200, 300: the local end of the connection, address and port.

\b \c{host} - the host name as given for the connection; a serial line's name (COM3); with proxy set and in 225, 325: the proxy's; 225, 325 local-command: the program's file name.

\b \c{kb} - 901: the kilobytes freed.

\b \c{keytype} - 210-213, 310-313: the host key's type as its fingerprint names it (ssh-ed25519, ssh-rsa, ...), rsa1 for an SSH-1 key, empty in a 213, 313 refused; 400: the key's SSH type.

\b \c{loaded} - 113: startup keys loaded.

\b \c{local} - 240, 241, 330, 331: the file's full local path; a 331 for a run that failed before any file: the local path as given.

\b \c{mb} - 901: LogKeepMB as set, 0 = off.

\b \c{method} - 220, 221, 320, 321: the authentication method; for 221 and 321 the one refused, or the last one tried when no method was left; values: none, publickey, password, keyboard-interactive, gssapi-with-mic, over SSH-1 also tis and cryptocard; for a proxy's login: password, chap, none, ident; 240, 241: zmodem or kitten-osc5113.

\b \c{methods} - 221, 321: the methods the server still offered, comma-separated (over SSH-1 from its authentication mask: publickey, password, tis, cryptocard); empty for a proxy's login.

\b \c{missing} - 902: each missing entry point with its DLL and the feature it powers, separated by semicolons.

\b \c{oldfp} - 213, 313: the hash of the stored key a replaced key took the place of (SHA256:...), empty for every other result.

\b \c{path} - 100-170: the key file; 401-403: the file written; 903: the session file.

\b \c{pattern} - 901: the folder and the log file name pattern searched.

\b \c{pid} - 100-170: the process that asked the agent, empty when none did; 200-403: the process writing the record.

\b \c{port} - the port connected to; a serial line's speed; with proxy set and in 225, 325: the proxy's; 225, 325 local-command: empty.

\b \c{program} - 900: the refused program file's path.

\b \c{protection} - 401, 403: none, passphrase or hello.

\b \c{proto} - 200, 300: the protocol; values: ssh, telnet, raw, rlogin, supdup, serial.

\b \c{proxy} - 210-221, 310-321: empty for the connection's own host key and login; for a proxy's its type: ssh (a jump host), http, socks5, socks4; 225, 325: the proxy's type: http, socks4, socks5, telnet, local-command.

\b \c{reason} - 100-170: a token - gui, cmdline, ipc, ipc-policy, tray, lifetime, device-removal, idle, windows-lock, windows-unlock, click-allow, click-deny, click-cancel-latch, pileup, suppress-latch, hello-verified, hello-denied, hello-unavailable, hello-error; 201, 301: the fatal error's text; 221, 321: access denied, public-key signature refused, no supported authentication methods available, the server's message when it ended the connection instead of answering, or a proxy's refusal as text; 230, 241, 331, 401, 402, 903: the reason as text.

\b \c{refused} - 113: startup keys refused.

\b \c{remote} - 240, 241, 330, 331: the file's remote path - in full where the protocol names it (sftp), else as the server sent it (scp protocol: the name; ZModem download: the name rz announced, or empty; kitten: the far end's name).

\b \c{req} - 100-170: the file name of the program that asked the agent.

\b \c{reqpath} - 100-170: that program's full path.

\b \c{request} - 230: what the far end asked for; values: osc52-read, osc5522-read, far2l-clipboard, file-read, file-write.

\b \c{result} - the outcome; 100, 101: allowed, denied; 110, 114, 115: done, blocked; 111: loaded, failed, fp-refused, not-verified; 112: forgotten; 120, 121: done, refused, waiting, unlock-shut, shut, blocked; 130: added, denied, failed; 131: protected, denied, failed, startup-entry-replaced; 132: hello, hello-cached, recovery-passphrase, printed-secret, denied, no-door-here, failed; 150, 151: done, failed; 152: done, failed (a wrong passphrase), cancelled; 160: start, stop; 170: failed; 201, 301: closed, remote-closed, fatal, user; 211, 212, 311, 312: accept-new, accepted, refused; 213, 313: stored, replaced, removed, proof-failed, refused (the server refused the proof request); 401, 402: saved, failed.

\b \c{session} - the saved session's name, empty when none was loaded.

\b \c{tool} - 400-403: kittygen or kittygen-cli.

\b \c{trigger} - 113: what started the retry; values: button, device-arrival; 152: what asked for the passphrase; values: first-use (a signature), gui (the key list's Decrypt).

\b \c{user} - 220, 221, 320, 321, 240, 241, 330, 331: the user name of the login (a proxy's: the name sent to it); 225, 325: the user name sent to the proxy, empty when none.

\b \c{warning} - 140: weak-protection or old-format.

\# END generated glossary

The event IDs:

\# BEGIN rows generated by tools/check-kitty-events.py --write-appendix

\b \c{0} \c{KiTTY++} (the line's own level): the whole text as \c{%1}.

\b \c{100} \c{KiTTY++_agent} (Information; Warning for a refusal or failure): \c{sign}, then \c{fp}, \c{comment}, \c{result}, \c{reason}, \c{req}, \c{reqpath}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{101} \c{KiTTY++_agent} (Information; Warning for a refusal or failure): \c{confirm}, then \c{fp}, \c{comment}, \c{result}, \c{reason}, \c{req}, \c{reqpath}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{110} \c{KiTTY++_agent} (Information; Warning for a refusal or failure): \c{add}, then \c{fp}, \c{comment}, \c{result}, \c{reason}, \c{req}, \c{reqpath}, \c{pid}, \c{path}.

\b \c{111} \c{KiTTY++_agent} (Information; Warning for a refusal or failure): \c{loadkey}, then \c{path}, \c{result}, \c{enc}.

\b \c{112} \c{KiTTY++_agent} (Information; Warning for a refusal or failure): \c{forget-path}, then \c{path}, \c{result}.

\b \c{113} \c{KiTTY++_agent} (Information; Warning for a refusal or failure): \c{retry}, then \c{trigger}, \c{loaded}, \c{refused}, \c{absent}, \c{broken}.

\b \c{114} \c{KiTTY++_agent} (Information; Warning for a refusal or failure): \c{remove}, then \c{fp}, \c{comment}, \c{result}, \c{reason}, \c{req}, \c{reqpath}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{115} \c{KiTTY++_agent} (Information; Warning for a refusal or failure): \c{remove-all}, then \c{fp}, \c{comment}, \c{result}, \c{reason}, \c{req}, \c{reqpath}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{120} \c{KiTTY++_agent} (Information; Warning for a refusal or failure): \c{lock}, then \c{fp}, \c{comment}, \c{result}, \c{reason}, \c{req}, \c{reqpath}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{121} \c{KiTTY++_agent} (Information; Warning for a refusal or failure): \c{unlock}, then \c{fp}, \c{comment}, \c{result}, \c{reason}, \c{req}, \c{reqpath}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{130} \c{KiTTY++_agent} (Information; Warning for a refusal or failure): \c{hello-enrol}, then \c{path}, \c{result}, \c{detail}.

\b \c{131} \c{KiTTY++_agent} (Information; Warning for a refusal or failure): \c{hello-protect}, then \c{path}, \c{dest}, \c{result}, \c{detail}, \c{err}.

\b \c{132} \c{KiTTY++_agent} (Information; Warning for a refusal or failure): \c{hello-unlock}, then \c{path}, \c{result}, \c{detail}.

\b \c{140} \c{KiTTY++_agent} (Warning): \c{keyfile-warning}, then \c{path}, \c{warning}.

\b \c{150} \c{KiTTY++_agent} (Information; Warning for a refusal or failure): \c{reencrypt-all}, then \c{fp}, \c{comment}, \c{result}, \c{reason}, \c{req}, \c{reqpath}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{151} \c{KiTTY++_agent} (Information; Warning for a refusal or failure): \c{reencrypt}, then \c{fp}, \c{comment}, \c{result}, \c{reason}, \c{req}, \c{reqpath}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{152} \c{KiTTY++_agent} (Information; Warning for a refusal or failure): \c{decrypt}, then \c{fp}, \c{comment}, \c{result}, \c{trigger}, \c{req}, \c{reqpath}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{160} \c{KiTTY++_agent} (Information; Warning for a refusal or failure): \c{agent}, then \c{result}.

\b \c{170} \c{KiTTY++_agent} (Information; Warning for a refusal or failure): \c{logrotate}, then \c{result}.

\b \c{200} \c{KiTTY++_kitty} (Information): \c{session-open}, then \c{session}, \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{proto}, \c{addr}, \c{from}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{201} \c{KiTTY++_kitty} (Information; Warning when fatal): \c{session-close}, then \c{session}, \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{result}, \c{reason}, \c{exitcode}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{210} \c{KiTTY++_kitty} (Information): \c{hostkey-known}, then \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{keytype}, \c{fp}, \c{basis}, \c{pid}, \c{proxy}.

\b \c{211} \c{KiTTY++_kitty} (Information; Warning when refused): \c{hostkey-new}, then \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{keytype}, \c{fp}, \c{result}, \c{pid}, \c{proxy}.

\b \c{212} \c{KiTTY++_kitty} (Warning): \c{hostkey-mismatch}, then \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{keytype}, \c{fp}, \c{result}, \c{pid}, \c{proxy}.

\b \c{213} \c{KiTTY++_kitty} (Information; Warning when proof-failed or refused): \c{hostkey-update}, then \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{keytype}, \c{fp}, \c{result}, \c{oldfp}, \c{pid}, \c{proxy}.

\b \c{220} \c{KiTTY++_kitty} (Information): \c{auth-ok}, then \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{user}, \c{method}, \c{fp}, \c{pid}, \c{proxy}, \c{for}.

\b \c{221} \c{KiTTY++_kitty} (Warning): \c{auth-failed}, then \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{user}, \c{method}, \c{reason}, \c{methods}, \c{pid}, \c{proxy}, \c{for}.

\b \c{225} \c{KiTTY++_kitty} (Information): \c{proxy-used}, then \c{proxy}, \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{user}, \c{credentials}, \c{pid}, \c{for}.

\b \c{230} \c{KiTTY++_kitty} (Warning): \c{farend-refused}, then \c{session}, \c{host}, \c{request}, \c{reason}, \c{detail}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{240} \c{KiTTY++_kitty} (Information): \c{transfer-done}, then \c{session}, \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{user}, \c{method}, \c{direction}, \c{local}, \c{remote}, \c{bytes}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{241} \c{KiTTY++_kitty} (Warning): \c{transfer-failed}, then \c{session}, \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{user}, \c{method}, \c{direction}, \c{local}, \c{remote}, \c{bytes}, \c{pid}, \c{reason}.

\b \c{300} \c{KiTTY++_cli} (Information): \c{session-open}, then \c{session}, \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{proto}, \c{addr}, \c{from}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{301} \c{KiTTY++_cli} (Information; Warning when fatal): \c{session-close}, then \c{session}, \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{result}, \c{reason}, \c{exitcode}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{310} \c{KiTTY++_cli} (Information): \c{hostkey-known}, then \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{keytype}, \c{fp}, \c{basis}, \c{pid}, \c{proxy}.

\b \c{311} \c{KiTTY++_cli} (Information; Warning when refused): \c{hostkey-new}, then \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{keytype}, \c{fp}, \c{result}, \c{pid}, \c{proxy}.

\b \c{312} \c{KiTTY++_cli} (Warning): \c{hostkey-mismatch}, then \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{keytype}, \c{fp}, \c{result}, \c{pid}, \c{proxy}.

\b \c{313} \c{KiTTY++_cli} (Information; Warning when proof-failed or refused): \c{hostkey-update}, then \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{keytype}, \c{fp}, \c{result}, \c{oldfp}, \c{pid}, \c{proxy}.

\b \c{320} \c{KiTTY++_cli} (Information): \c{auth-ok}, then \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{user}, \c{method}, \c{fp}, \c{pid}, \c{proxy}, \c{for}.

\b \c{321} \c{KiTTY++_cli} (Warning): \c{auth-failed}, then \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{user}, \c{method}, \c{reason}, \c{methods}, \c{pid}, \c{proxy}, \c{for}.

\b \c{325} \c{KiTTY++_cli} (Information): \c{proxy-used}, then \c{proxy}, \c{host}, \c{port}, \c{user}, \c{credentials}, \c{pid}, \c{for}.

\b \c{330} \c{KiTTY++_cli} (Information): \c{transfer-done}, then \c{session}, \c{host}, \c{user}, \c{direction}, \c{local}, \c{remote}, \c{bytes}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{331} \c{KiTTY++_cli} (Warning): \c{transfer-failed}, then \c{session}, \c{host}, \c{user}, \c{direction}, \c{local}, \c{remote}, \c{bytes}, \c{pid}, \c{reason}.

\b \c{400} \c{KiTTY++_kittygen} (Information): \c{key-generated}, then \c{tool}, \c{keytype}, \c{bits}, \c{fp}, \c{comment}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{401} \c{KiTTY++_kittygen} (Information; Warning when failed): \c{private-saved}, then \c{tool}, \c{fp}, \c{comment}, \c{path}, \c{format}, \c{protection}, \c{result}, \c{reason}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{402} \c{KiTTY++_kittygen} (Information; Warning when failed): \c{public-saved}, then \c{tool}, \c{fp}, \c{path}, \c{format}, \c{result}, \c{reason}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{403} \c{KiTTY++_kittygen} (Information): \c{passphrase-changed}, then \c{tool}, \c{fp}, \c{path}, \c{protection}, \c{pid}.

\b \c{900} \c{KiTTY++} (Error): \c{program-refused}, then \c{check}, \c{found}, \c{program}.

\b \c{901} \c{KiTTY++} (Information): \c{log-retention}, then \c{files}, \c{kb}, \c{days}, \c{mb}, \c{pattern}.

\b \c{902} \c{KiTTY++} (Information): \c{missing-features}, then \c{features}, \c{missing}.

\b \c{903} \c{KiTTY++} (Warning): \c{session-save-failed}, then \c{session}, \c{path}, \c{reason}.

